---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
---
<Site
  title="About · Ouijit"
  description="Ouijit is built by one person, Prentice Bjerkeseth. Free, open source under AGPL, no account and no telemetry, and the plan is to keep it that way.">
  <main class="compare-content about-content">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      Ouijit is built by one person. I'm <a href="https://github.com/pbjer" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Prentice Bjerkeseth</a>,
      and every commit is mine.
    </p>
    <p>
      It started as having fun building something with AI once AI got good enough to build with. Within a week
      it was the only way I worked, because a terminal manager starts out exactly as capable as the agents it
      runs. That is still the position: capabilities and tooling move fastest at the terminal, so Ouijit wraps
      around the agent's own CLI rather than replacing it. A chat interface is coming, but the terminal stays
      underneath.
    </p>
    <p>
      Ouijit is free. If it ever has a price, it will be for additive features that cost something to operate
      beyond my time, such as servers for cloud environments or syncing. The app itself will not be the thing
      that costs money.
    </p>
    <p>
      There is no account, no sign-in and no telemetry. I don't think a tool like this should require a login,
      and I don't think you should have to give up privacy to get high quality tools. The only usage number I
      have is how many times each build has been downloaded.
    </p>
    <p>
      The code is open source under AGPL-3.0. I wanted it open, and I didn't want a company to take the work
      and profit from it easily.
    </p>
    <p>
      Tools in this space are raising venture money, being acquired, or shutting down. The plan for Ouijit is
      to still be standing, still free and still private, and to show that an individual can build something
      special here.
    </p>
  </main>
</Site>
